  "body": "## Cause\n\nThe stock preview march stopped after 64 steps (`crates/ui/src/trace.wgsl` and its CPU twin `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/preview/march.rs`). Over a flat face, each step is 0.9 x the height above the face. Thus a ray at a small angle to a faced floor comes near the floor slowly. At 64 steps, the ray got status 2 (no verdict). `composite.wgsl` discards each pixel that is not a hit, so the grid showed through the stock.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `MAX_STEPS` is 256 in the two twins (it was 64).\n- New exhaustion verdict in the two twins (`exhausted`). A ray that uses all its steps gets a hit only when material is proved on the ray:\n  - the last sample is inside, or\n  - the sample one cell further along the ray is inside (the probe of the existing hit law).\n- Then 6 bisections of that one-cell bracket put the hit within 1/64 cell of the surface, on the material side (`BISECT`).\n- Each other exhausted ray keeps status 2. A near miss is never painted.\n- The hit law, the miss law and `composite.wgsl` do not change.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3612-preview-march-steps.md`.\n\n## Readings (CPU twin)\n\nFixture: a 10 x 10 x 5 box on 1 mm cells, faced to z 4.5 with a flat r 2 tool. The frame is 64 x 64. The eye is 30 mm from the floor centre. The table gives the rays with no verdict, for each step cap, before the fallback:\n\n| Angle above the floor | 64 (old) | 96 | 128 | 192 | 256 | 512 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 60 deg | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| 30 deg | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| 10 deg | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| 5 deg | 70 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| 3 deg | 152 | 42 | 6 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| 2 deg | 166 | 62 | 6 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| 1 deg | 112 | 70 | 64 | 24 | 0 | 0 |\n\n- At 64, rays that surely meet the box read as a miss: 5 deg 8, 3 deg 68, 2 deg 30. After the fix: 0 at each angle.\n- Rays that surely miss the box and are painted: 0 at each cap, with and without the fallback.\n- The fallback alone at 64: 5 deg 70 -> 32, 3 deg 152 -> 56. It cannot help a ray that passes above the floor and misses. That ray keeps status 2, which is correct.\n- After the fix (256 + fallback): 0 unresolved from 60 deg down to 1 deg. At 0.5 deg, 16 rays have no verdict, and none of them is a sure hit.\n- CPU preview time of the fixture (debug, whole frame with the column cache): 1 deg view 577 ms at 64 -> 643-661 ms at 256 (about +11 %). The other views are in the noise. On the GPU, only the pixels that used to run out pay for the extra steps.\n\n## Pinning test\n\n- `crates/sim/tests/stock_preview.rs`: `a_grazing_faced_floor_resolves_and_stays_see_through`. It compares each ray with an analytic box silhouette (one cell of slack):\n  - From 60 deg to 1 deg: 0 unresolved, and no sure hit reads as a miss.\n  - At each angle, 0.5 deg included: no sure miss is painted.\n  - At 64 steps, this test fails (see the table).\n\n## Gate (head 12c6d0805)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-sim -j 6`: 95 binaries, 857 passed, 0 failed.\n- `CAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU=1 cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test trace_parity -- --test-threads=1`: 5 passed. The tests ran on an adapter (with the variable set, a missing adapter is an error, not a skip). `gpu.unresolved == cpu.unresolved` stays green.\n- Same for `--test trace_composite`: 5 passed. `--test gpu_render`: 19 passed, 1 ignored.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -j 6`: 1516 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `-p camcraft-ui --all-targets`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No app window was opened. The picture of the user is not reproduced on screen. The fix is shown on the CPU twin and by the GPU parity test.\n- `trace_parity` and `trace_composite` have no GPU lock (#3605). This PR does not change these files. I ran them with `--test-threads=1`.\n- No heavy lane. This is a P3 PR.\n\nChangelog: The cut stock preview no longer shows holes on a faced floor at a low view angle: the march takes up to 256 steps and gives a hit only where material is proved on the ray.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #3612\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
